  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000009: iterated_2opt_perturbation\n\nStatus: timeout; distance: 1e+06\n\nThought: Construct initial tour via nearest neighbor, then repeatedly apply 2-opt until local optimum, perturb with random double-bridge move, and re-optimize. Keep best tour found.\n\nError details: timeout on tsp_construct_500_seed2024_000: Solver timed out after 60.0015s (timeout_seconds=60)\n\nHistory source: yes\nHistory bucket: tsp:size:500\nHistory role: regime specialist\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef two_opt(tour, dist):\n    n = len(tour)\n    improved = True\n    while improved:\n        improved = False\n        for i in range(n-2):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                a, b = tour[i], tour[i+1]\n                c, d = tour[j], tour[(j+1)%n]\n                if dist[a,c] + dist[b,d] < dist[a,b] + dist[c,d] - 1e-10:\n                    tour[i+1:j+1] = tour[i+1:j+1][::-1]\n                    improved = True\n                    break\n            if improved:\n                break\n    cost = dist[tour[-1], tour[0]] + np.sum(dist[tour[:-1], tour[1:]])\n    return tour, cost\n\ndef double_bridge(tour, rng):\n    n = len(tour)\n    if n < 4:\n        return tour\n    i = rng.integers(1, max(2, n//3))\n    j = rng.integers(i+1, min(i + n//3, n-2))\n    k = rng.integers(j+1, min(j + n//3, n-1))\n    A = tour[:i]\n    B = tour[i:j]\n    C = tour[j:k]\n    D = tour[k:]\n    new_tour = np.concatenate([A, C, B, D])\n    return new_tour\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix):\n    n = distance_matrix.shape[0]\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.array([])\n    if n == 1:\n        return np.array([0])\n    if n == 2:\n        return np.array([0,1])\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    # nearest neighbor construction\n    tour = [0]\n    unvisited = set(range(1,n))\n    cur = 0\n    while unvisited:\n        nxt = min(unvisited, key=lambda c: distance_matrix[cur,c])\n        tour.append(nxt)\n        unvisited.remove(nxt)\n        cur = nxt\n    tour = np.array(tour, dtype=int)\n    best_cost = distance_matrix[tour[-1], tour[0]] + np.sum(distance_matrix[tour[:-1], tour[1:]])\n    best_tour = tour.copy()\n    report_best_tour(best_tour)\n    # improve with 2-opt\n    tour, cost = two_opt(tour.copy(), distance_matrix)\n    if cost < best_cost - 1e-10:\n        best_cost = cost\n        best_tour = tour.copy()\n        report_best_tour(best_tour)\n    # iterated local search with perturbation\n    for _ in range(20):\n        perturbed = double_bridge(tour.copy(), rng)\n        improved_tour, improved_cost = two_opt(perturbed, distance_matrix)\n        if improved_cost < best_cost - 1e-10:\n            best_cost = improved_cost\n            best_tour = improved_tour.copy()\n            report_best_tour(best_tour)\n        tour = improved_tour\n    return best_tour\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000009 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Candidate timed out on 70% of 500-city runs (mean runtime ~57s), while robust parents completed all runs within 25s, indicating ILS with 20 two-opt iterations is too slow.\n- Aim: Reduce runtime to under 60s for 500-city instances by limiting the number of local search iterations per restart or substituting with a cheaper local search.\n- Preserve: Nearest-neighbor construction; 2-opt improvement (with cost or iteration cap); report_best_tour on improvements\n- Change: Replace the 20-iteration ILS loop with a fixed small number (e.g., 5) of restarts without perturbation; Or use a single 2-opt pass with a limit on improving moves\n- Avoid: Adding additional loops or complex perturbations that increase runtime; Breaking permutation